«
@@ ============================================================
@@ Sextant — observed altitude from a sextant altitude: index correction, dip of
@@ the horizon, refraction, semidiameter and parallax.
@@ 
@@ Input : Hs IC h SD HP — sextant altitude; index correction; height of eye;
@@         semidiameter, positive for the lower limb, negative for the upper limb,
@@         zero for a star; horizontal parallax. Plain numbers are degrees for Hs,
@@         arc minutes for IC, SD and HP, metres for h; units are accepted.
@@ Output: Ho — observed altitude.
@@ Dip 1.76′√h, as in Bowditch appendix B with h in metres. Refraction by the
@@ formula of G. G. Bennett (1982), for standard air. With a bubble sextant, h is 0.
@@ Angle mode and angle units setting are restored before returning.
@@ ============================================================

  3 PICK DROP
  → hps ice hgt sdm hpr
  «
    hps →Num IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_° CONVERT UVAL END
    ice →Num IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_arcmin CONVERT UVAL END
    hgt IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_m CONVERT UVAL END →Num
    sdm →Num IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_arcmin CONVERT UVAL END
    hpr →Num IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_arcmin CONVERT UVAL END
    'AngleMode' RCL 'SetAngleUnits' RCL
    RAD NoAngleUnits
    Ⓒπ →Num 180 /
    → hsx icx hmx sdx hpx amode aunits rdn
    «
      IF hmx 0 < THEN "Height of eye must not be negative" DOERR END
      'hsx+(icx-1.76*√hmx)/60' EVAL
      → hap
      «
        'hap+(sdx+hpx*COS(hap*rdn)-1/TAN((hap+7.31/(hap+4.4))*rdn))/60' EVAL 1_° *
      »
      amode EVAL IF aunits THEN SetAngleUnits ELSE NoAngleUnits END
    »
  »
»
